+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+When closing fast on a stopped or slow lead that is still far, the plan follows a stop target at a constant deceleration fixed when the lead is first seen, so braking starts earlier and softer. Only the cost reference and weight change; obstacles and the danger constraint stay as they are.
+
+- **On:** It starts when ego closes at 15 km/h or more on a lead at 15 km/h or less (or one predicted to stop) with a time gap of at least 1.5 s. The deceleration is 1.1 times what stops ego at the stop distance behind the lead at that moment (at least 0.5 m/s²), applied over 1 s. It does not start when that exceeds 2.0 m/s² or when the lead is clearly pulling away.
+- **Off:** Nothing is computed; behavior is unchanged.
+- **Release:** It fades out over 0.5 s when the lead pulls away (while 30 m or more ahead) or speeds up, or ego stops closing. A lead change, driver brake or accelerator input, or longitudinal control off ends it at once.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+Turn it on when the car keeps the set speed toward a stopped car seen from far and then brakes late. Changes while driving apply within about 5 s without restarting.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+<!-- CARROT:NOTICE level="WARNING" -->
+> [!WARNING]
+> Experimental and not validated on a vehicle. In log replay of 15 stopped-lead approaches, the median braking-start distance rose from 48.8 to 56.4 m and the median peak deceleration fell from -2.06 to -1.77 m/s², with stops at 3.31–4.07 m. A lead detected late or braking hard gets the same braking as before.
+<!-- CARROT:NOTICE:END -->
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
 <!-- CARROT:MANUAL:END ApproachSoftStop -->
 
